    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d607">

                <pb facs="1063" n="1049" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1049"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/6139b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)<anchor n="34" xml:id="d607-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-25T13:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1805. The following is for Harrison and McClelland and is WRB cable no. 26.</p>
                <p>Systematic mass-extermination of Jews in Hungary has begun according to
                    persistent and seemingly authentic reports. The presence in Hungary of the
                    largest possible number of foreign observers may cause restraint which will
                    directly affect the lives of 800,000 human beings in that country. Please urge,
                    with this end in view, appropriate authorities to take immediate steps in
                    interest of humanity to enlarge to greatest possible extent the numbers of Swiss
                    diplomatic and consular <pb facs="1064" n="1050" xml:id="pg1050"/> personnel in
                    Hungary and to distribute them throughout the country as widely as possible.</p>
                <p>All such diplomatic and consular representatives will use, it is hoped, all
                    available means to urge desisting from further barbarism upon officials and
                    private individuals. The Department should be informed immediately of extent of
                    cooperation of Swiss Government.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d607-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d607-f1" n="34" type="source" xml:id="d607-f1-content">
                <p>Substantially the same message was sent on the same date to Ankara (No. 468),
                    Lisbon (No. 1479), and Stockholm (No. 1010); on May 26 to Madrid (No. 1515).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d607-f2" n="35" xml:id="d607-f2-content">
                <p>Switzerland was not persuaded to increase its diplomatic personnel in Hungary.
                    Only in the case of Sweden was the proposal accepted; the Swedish Foreign Office
                    appointed a Special Attaché to the Swedish Legation at Budapest (Wallenberg),
                    and shortly after his arrival there, it was reported that several thousand
                    persons were placed under effective Swedish protection.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
